Package: cloneCallR
Title: Tools For Clone Calling Using demuxmix Posteriors And A Naive Bayes Classifier
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: 
    person("Sam", "Lee", , "samleenz@me.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Combinatorial barcodes allow us to efficiently create labelled populations for sample multiplexing or, more likely, lineage tracing experiments. Regular demultiplexing tools however cannot be used as they assume a one-to-one mapping between barcodes and samples. cloneCallR implements a naive Bayes classifier that uses the posterior probabilities from demuxmix to assign cells to clones based on a known barcode-clone mapping.
